media: i2c: ov5693: pin the sensor to its native mode, the binned one stalls

On a Surface Pro 5 (1796) with linux-surface 6.19.8, the front camera streams
perfectly when libcamera drives it directly -- `cam -c2 --capture=5` gives
28.5 fps at 1280x720 -- but produces *nothing* when an application asks for it
through PipeWire (Kamoso, Chrome/webcamtests). The kernel says, on every try:

    ipu3-cio2: CSI-2 receiver port 1: frame sync error
    ipu3-cio2: payload length is 1617408, received 0

(the sensor's power LED comes on, so the sensor is powered: it just never
delivers a byte). The difference between the two runs is the *sensor mode*,
visible on the CSI-2 link with media-ctl:

    direct (works)      : SBGGR10_1X10/2592x1944   <- native
    via an application  : SBGGR10_1X10/1296x972    <- binned 2x2

ov5693_set_fmt() derives that binning from the requested size:

    hratio = clamp_t(..., DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->width,  width), 1, 2);
    vratio = clamp_t(..., DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->height, height), 1, 2);

a 1280x720 request gives hratio = round(2592/1280) = 2 and
vratio = round(1944/720) = 3 -> clamped to 2, hence the 1296x972 output. And
1280x720 is exactly what every application asks for, because the IPU3 pipeline
caps all its cameras at that size and libcamera picks the smallest mode >= the
request. So every application lands on the binned mode.

Why the direct path escapes it is libcamera's business (it configures the
sensor at its default 2592x1944 rather than at the requested size); what
matters here is that the binned output does not stream on this sensor/bridge
combination. Pin hratio and vratio to 1 so the sensor always runs its native
2592x1944 mode, whatever size the caller asks for; the IMGU downsamples
(2.03x for a 1280x720 request). This is the same remedy, for the same reason,
as 0003 does for the ov8865's non-native modes.

Cost: the sensor always runs 2592x1944 (slightly more power, IMGU always
downsamples), and a caller asking for a *smaller* size than the crop now gets
2592x1944 instead of a binned 1296x972 -- which is the point.

Applies to : linux v6.19.x, drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
Apply with : patch -p1 < 0004-...patch     (run from the kernel tree root)

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
@@ -814,29 +814,34 @@
 	const struct v4l2_rect *crop;
 	struct v4l2_mbus_framefmt *fmt;
 	unsigned int hratio, vratio;
-	unsigned int width, height;
 	unsigned int hblank;
 	int exposure_max;
 
 	crop = __ov5693_get_pad_crop(ov5693, state, format->pad, format->which);
 
 	/*
-	 * Align to two to simplify the binning calculations below, and clamp
-	 * the requested format at the crop rectangle
+	 * Surface Pro 5 / IPU3 workaround: the 2x2 binned path does not stream.
+	 *
+	 * Measured on a Surface Pro 5 (1796) running linux-surface 6.19.8: a
+	 * request for 1280x720 -- which is what libcamera hands this sensor,
+	 * because the IPU3 pipeline caps every camera at that size -- used to
+	 * select the binned output 1296x972 (hratio/vratio == 2). The CSI-2
+	 * receiver then reported
+	 *
+	 *   ipu3-cio2: CSI-2 receiver port 1: frame sync error
+	 *   ipu3-cio2: payload length is 1617408, received 0
+	 *
+	 * i.e. not a single byte, while the sensor's own power LED came on.
+	 * The native 2592x1944 mode (hratio/vratio == 1) streams at 28.5 fps.
+	 * libcamera picks the smallest size >= the request, so every
+	 * application lands on the broken binned mode.
+	 *
+	 * Pin the sensor to its native mode whatever the caller asks for; the
+	 * IMGU downsamples for smaller requests. Same remedy as the ov8865
+	 * non-native modes on this platform.
 	 */
-	width = clamp_t(unsigned int, ALIGN(format->format.width, 2),
-			OV5693_MIN_CROP_WIDTH, crop->width);
-	height = clamp_t(unsigned int, ALIGN(format->format.height, 2),
-			 OV5693_MIN_CROP_HEIGHT, crop->height);
-
-	/*
-	 * We can only support setting either the dimensions of the crop rect
-	 * or those dimensions binned (separately) by a factor of two.
-	 */
-	hratio = clamp_t(unsigned int,
-			 DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->width, width), 1, 2);
-	vratio = clamp_t(unsigned int,
-			 DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(crop->height, height), 1, 2);
+	hratio = 1;
+	vratio = 1;
 
 	fmt = __ov5693_get_pad_format(ov5693, state, format->pad,
 				      format->which);
